// The program of the package `wakeups`, its guard: every file of the package
// but the tests, with no Bun and no Node types, and a `lib` of `ESNext` only.
// `tsc` follows imports, so a file passes only if all that it imports passes
// too. It lists the core's file of declarations, `../core/tsconfig.core.d.ts`
// (what the core may use, so that a file that imports the core passes). So
// the guard refuses a module of Bun or of Node that no declaration names, and
// passes what that file names, the core's `node:crypto` too. What refuses
// each module of Bun or of Node in the package's files is the list of
// built-ins of `tools/graph.ts` (`BUILTINS`), which gives them none. The
// tests are checked with the Bun types, by `tsconfig.test.json`.
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ESNext"],
    "types": []
  },
  "files": ["../core/tsconfig.core.d.ts"],
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts"]
}
